  "ai": {
    "status": "ok",
    "model": "deepseek-chat",
    "summary": "Release is blocked: the change replaces Deployment/demo/demo spec.replicas with 0 (REPLICAS_ZERO, BLOCK), which is not an approved release. The decision preview is BLOCK and must stand. Two REVIEW findings also warrant attention before any re-submission: 35 scheduled Pods lack CPU/memory requests, so free capacity (2190m CPU, ~9.2GB memory on 1 ready worker) may be overstated, and the KubeCPUOvercommit alert is firing. Note that the current Deployment still shows 1 ready replica, so the zero-replica state is the proposed change, not observed availability; do not treat the existing Ready Pod as evidence the release is safe. Any fault-injection settings (e.g. DEMO_STARTUP_FAIL, DEMO_ERROR_RATE) must not appear in the candidate manifest.",
    "additional_risks": [
      {
        "title": "Zero-replica change removes serving capacity",
        "detail": "The proposed replace sets spec.replicas to 0 for Deployment/demo/demo. This is a hard BLOCK and must not be approved; a rollout to zero replicas would take the workload out of service rather than exercise rolling-update protection.",
        "severity": "REVIEW"
      },
      {
        "title": "Capacity estimate unreliable due to unreserved Pod requests",
        "detail": "35 scheduled Pods have no CPU/memory requests and are counted as zero, so the reported free capacity may be overstated. Combined with a firing KubeCPUOvercommit alert, capacity headroom should be re-verified before any resubmission.",
